<html>
<body>
<h2>JavaScript arrya methods></h2>
<p>the joind() method joins arrya elements into a string and the pop() method removes the last element from an arrya.</p>
<p id="myjoin"></p>
<p id="myfirstpop"></p>
<p id="mysecondpop"></p>
<script>
var fruits = ["banana", "orange", "apple", "mango"];
document.getElementById("myjoin").innerHTML= fruits.join("*");
document.getElementById("myfirstpop").innerHTML= fruits;fruits.pop();
document.getElementById("mysecondpop").innerHTML= fruits;
</script>
</body>
</html>